  "known_limitations": [
    "scope of proof: installation outside the checkout, governed admission of a real model patch on a real consumer, and vitest+DOM acceptance; NOT proof that LSP or DAP guided the correction",
    "the defect and its two class names are quoted in the specification sent to the model; the swap is trivial",
    "the governed verifier is a regex over the .tsx that repeats the specification; vitest runs outside the governed sandbox because the contract mounts node_modules only through the pnpm virtual store",
    "DAP debugged a reproducer of the harness that extracts and evaluates the class expression, not the component",
    "the browser of A renders a harness preview page with two real StatsCard, not the real route of the app (it needs authentication and an API); the defective state of A is captured in screenshots/A-defective.png for comparison",
    "LSP: the defect is not a type error; hover inside the JSX template returns any; diagnostics (85) include dependency-type noise",
    "B is synthetic (test, defect and requirement created by the journey); in the browser it needed VITE_API_BASE empty at build time and one third-party font tag removed from the served HTML copy (source untouched)",
    "vitest 1.6.1 with only --maxWorkers=2 fails with \"minThreads and maxThreads must not conflict\", runs no test and exits 0 (false green); the journey uses --maxWorkers=2 --minWorkers=1 and refuses a run with zero tests",
    "reviewProjectResult emits a whole-file patch (49 removed and 49 added lines in A, 129 and 129 in B) although the real difference is one line",
    "the Claude client in the cgroup PATH is 2.1.263, not the interactive 2.1.302; the adapter checks the version at inspection and it matched",
    "cost \"US$ 0\" is not measured: subscription receipts carry cost_microusd null; max_cost_microusd 0 forbids paid spend",
    "s05b reads the Codex account and quota through the codex app-server, which contacts the provider (network use not measured at socket level); no inference",
